        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Removes obsolete Node.js notes for <code class=\"notranslate\">SubtleCrypto</code> algorithms.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As of Node 20, those are no longer experimental.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #27964.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3440339582\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27964\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27964/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27964\">#27964</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28023",
            "title": "Remove experimental Node.js notes for `SubtleCrypto`",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-29T10:19:03.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-29T10:17:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2977353?u=16bc8a352fe2375d06afa25a6b6e3f56bbfa07dd&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I believe this was missed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3153512050\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27087\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27087/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27087\">#27087</a>. This was implemented in Safari 26 as part of the anchor positioning work.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tested adding a <code class=\"notranslate\">@position-try</code> rule to a CSS file on a website I built and it showed up as a valid rule in Safari 26:</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/2977353/494816642-d02056a6-9b73-49ee-bfc7-288d8ef00cd6.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..MnALxgP-YgpGocnG2bRaTlXkRlWHn7XSuKZMTTsOfpU\"><img width=\"1361\" height=\"525\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-09-27 at 9 28 32 PM\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/2977353/494816642-d02056a6-9b73-49ee-bfc7-288d8ef00cd6.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..MnALxgP-YgpGocnG2bRaTlXkRlWHn7XSuKZMTTsOfpU\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 525px;\"></a>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">See the WPT tests for @position-try in Safari:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-anchor-position/at-position-try-allowed-declarations.html?label=master&amp;product=chrome%5Bexperimental%5D&amp;product=edge%5Bexperimental%5D&amp;product=firefox%5Bexperimental%5D&amp;product=safari%5Bstable%5D&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">WPT tests for allowed declarations</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-anchor-position?label=master&amp;label=stable&amp;product=safari&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">WPT tests for anchor positioning overall, including many for \"at-position-try\"</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28017",
            "title": "Update Safari support for @position-try as it was implemented in Safari 26",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-28T03:49:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-28T03:29:43.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "connorshea",
                "url": "https://github.com/connorshea"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 140 adds support for <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/css-values-4/#calc-type-checking\" rel=\"nofollow\">CSS typed arithmetic</a>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/4740780497043456\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/4740780497043456</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is not very clear what this is from the spec, but <a href=\"https://css-tricks.com/css-typed-arithmetic/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://css-tricks.com/css-typed-arithmetic/</a> provides a good explanation.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari also supports it. The relevant bug appears to be <a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=278244\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=278244</a>, which says Safari 18, but I've tried 18.5 and it doesn't work in that version. I upgraded to Safari 26, and it did work, so I've put the Safari support version down as 26.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In terms of what features this will be used in, it is mainly relevant to <code class=\"notranslate\">calc()</code>. <code class=\"notranslate\">abs()</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">sign()</code> also directly take a calculation/expression as a value, and I've tested it works on them, so I've included the data point on those functions as well.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In terms of including it in other function data, I don't know. I mean, you can technically use a <code class=\"notranslate\">calc()</code> just about anywhere that accepts numeric units, but I didn't think it was worth including it in other places as it would get confusing. Opinions welcome.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28006",
            "title": "Add subfeatures to indicate support for CSS typed arithmetic",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-26T16:56:42.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-26T16:55:46.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Declarative Push landed in the specifications, so now we can add it to BCD.<br>\n<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1891229019\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/w3c/push-api/issues/360\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/w3c/push-api/issues/360/hovercard?comment_id=3273779714&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/w3c/push-api/issues/360#issuecomment-3273779714\">w3c/push-api#360 (comment)</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm not sure if</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>this PR is complete. Maybe additional APIs come along with this, but this is what I collected from the OWD collector project for now</li>\n<li>it is in webview_ios (we usually default to mirror, which is what I did here, too).</li>\n<li>the note about Home Screen web apps makes sense</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28000",
            "title": "Add Declarative Push",
