        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 added support for <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582</a> , as updated in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3422725499\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27902\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27902/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27902\">#27902</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However as explained in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582#c30\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1919582#c30</a> the  <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> was renamed from a preexisting <code class=\"notranslate\">CSS2Properties</code>. This adds the alternative name to the feature for Firefox. Note that the developer indicates this was from version 2 (checked) but might have been version 1.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">FF145 added support for returning this from <code class=\"notranslate\">.style</code> in elements (HTML, SVG, MathML) and also in <code class=\"notranslate\">getComputedStyle()</code> in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925</a>. I have set these to have a subfeature indicating the new return type.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is not clear if FF returns it from <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleRule.style</code> - I am asking in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925#c4\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1989925#c4</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome hasn't added support for <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> as far as I can tell.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Safari has been marked as supporting  <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code> in 26 already, but the return methods were not marked. I have set all of them to working in that version though I have not tested it (they appear to be updated in source though, and 26 was the version the interface went in).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In addition, the spec changed to move the <code class=\"notranslate\">cssFloat</code> attribute from <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">CSSStyleProperties</code>. This won't affect FF which never implemented that, but it does affect Safari. So I've marked it as removed and also now non-standard and deprecated.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417388824\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41133/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133\">mdn/content#41133</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27975",
            "title": "FF144 CSSStyleProperties CSS2Properties",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-28T23:15:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-23T05:28:06.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 adds support for cross-origin <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;iframe&gt;</code> to require sticky activation and user permission before it can do <code class=\"notranslate\">Window.top</code> navigation (i.e. set <code class=\"notranslate\">top.location</code>) in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This was originally supported in Chrome 68 (<a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5851021045661696\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5851021045661696</a>) and Safari 13 (<a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=193076\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=193076</a>).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that this is not standard though AFAIK. There are discussions in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1272422076\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8013\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/issues/8013/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8013\">whatwg/html#8013</a> and all the main browsers comply, but no place to point in the HTML spec. Further there are tests, but these aren't all passed by anyone and are marked as experimental.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that according to <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501#c28\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1419501#c28</a> if the redirect is blocked then Chrome and FF will prompt for user permission to navigate and log the error in console, while Safari just blocks the navigation and reports and error in the dev console.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417409664\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41138\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41138/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41138\">mdn/content#41138</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27960",
            "title": "FF144 cross-origin iframe requires user interaction for top-navigation",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-28T22:52:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-22T03:22:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">And a note, as per <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26004#issuecomment-3303107033\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26004/hovercard\">feedback on the issue</a>, about issues with <code class=\"notranslate\">query</code> in Firefox for Android.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #26004.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2872228631\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26004\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26004/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/26004\">#26004</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27919",
            "title": "Issue-26004 webextensions.api.tabs.query on Firefox for Android",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-17T22:12:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-17T22:11:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43868318?u=3f179cacfd70db40ae7c11f1b951533a8ebf45bf&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added caret.json with compatibility data structure</li>\n<li>Currently no browser support, but Chrome support expected soon</li>\n<li>Marked as experimental and standard track</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27904",
            "title": "Add CSS caret property (WIP - awaiting browser support)",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-16T16:55:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-16T16:54:30.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "yashrajbharti",
                "url": "https://github.com/yashrajbharti"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 added a new constraint parameter <code class=\"notranslate\">resizeMode</code> for use with <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getUserMedia\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MediaDevices.getUserMedia()</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We haven't documented the constraints before so this attempts to do so as there are other compat differences.<br>\nThe results are based on the test <a href=\"https://wpt.live/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.live/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html</a>, and more specifically, by bisecting based on the wpt results using product tests like:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Chrome: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html?label=master&amp;product=chrome-80&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html?label=master&amp;product=chrome-80&amp;aligned</a></li>\n<li>Firefox <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html?label=master&amp;product=firefox-115&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html?label=master&amp;product=firefox-115&amp;aligned</a></li>\n<li>Safari <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html?label=master&amp;product=safari-12&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints.https.html?label=master&amp;product=safari-12&amp;aligned</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The tests and results do not run on the earliest version that constraints should be supported for, so I have used <code class=\"notranslate\">≤</code> to indicate the earliest version I could test in each case.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that there are some constraints I have not documented:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">backgroundBlur</code> is in spec but not in tests. Assuming it is not implemented though it might be.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">volume</code> is not in spec, but shows up in some very old builds. Ignoring.</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">voiceIsolation</code> is supported by Chrome but is not in spec. Ignoring.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that there a related test <a href=\"https://wpt.live/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getUserMedia.https.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.live/mediacapture-streams/MediaDevices-getUserMedia.https.html</a> but everything passes in this for things that support the associated constraint, so this does not lead to any compatibility difference to record.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3417378973\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41132/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41132\">mdn/content#41132</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27891",
            "title": "MediaDevices.getUserMedia() add constraints",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-26T00:06:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-16T02:27:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarified the behavior of the topSites permission on Android. The API that the permission enables was removed in Firefox for Android 68. Tested and confirmed, using the permissions example, on an Android device that:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>topSites can be specified as a permission, but has no effect.</li>\n<li>topSites can be specified as an optional permission, but if an attempt is made to grant it an error occurs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #23090.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2295533234\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23090\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23090/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23090\">#23090</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27823",
            "title": "Issue-23090 manifest.optional_permissions topSites on Android",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-10T18:39:18.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-10T18:38:36.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        }
